{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-1","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · DSH trace waterfall：A DeepSeek Harness plugin that replaces the trajectory view with a trace waterfall inspired by [Kobra](https://kobra.systems/components/trace-waterfall). The presentation is independently implemented; no Kobra code or assets are included.","source":"extracted","section":"DSH trace waterfall"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-2","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · DSH trace waterfall：- Turn rows show model, tool, waiting, handoff, and failed activity as one segmented bar.\n- A three-lane overview (input / model / tools) supports drag-to-zoom; long idle gaps collapse into axis breaks, and any turn can be focused.\n- Model bars split time to first token from decoding.\n- Click a row or bar for an anchored summary, then open full details for complete input, output, timing, and metadata.","source":"extracted","section":"DSH trace waterfall"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-3","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Video：https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe12bc0d-32b7-4761-8996-d7ae5887637a\n\nA 100-second tour: the built-in trajectory view for comparison, the main interactions, and a real agent run recorded live.","source":"extracted","section":"Video"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-4","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Install：Requires Node 24.9+ and pnpm 11 on `PATH` (`dsh plugin` uses pnpm; pnpm 10 fails with `ERR_PNPM_ADDING_TO_ROOT`). Tested with DSH **0.2.1-rc.5** and the 0.2.2-alpha line (master at `ce7073d`); DSH's plugin APIs are pre-stable.\n\nInstall from GitHub:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall\n```","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-5","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Install：The bundle's `cordis.patch.yml` disables `ui-trajectory` and adds `trace-waterfall`. The view ID stays `trajectory`, so existing view preferences and tool-inspection links keep working. Restart DSH Web or reload the browser after installing.\n\nTo update to the latest commit, run the same `add` command again.\n\nTo restore DSH's original trace:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-trace-waterfall\n```\n\nDo not enable both trajectory providers at once; they own the same view.","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-6","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Develop：Requires a built DeepSeek Harness checkout of `master` or `dsh-v0.2.2-alpha.2` and later. The 0.2.1 release line still runs the plugin, but `tsc` fails there because the PTC event types live in `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` instead of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-executor-ptc`.\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm run link:dsh -- <path-to-deepseek-harness>\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n\n`link:dsh` links the DSH packages and generates TypeScript paths; rerun it after reinstalling dependencies or switching checkouts.","source":"extracted","section":"Develop"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-7","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Develop：The built `lib/` is committed so that GitHub installs need no build step. Run `npm run build` and commit `lib/` together with source changes.\n\nTo install your working copy instead of the GitHub version, run `dsh plugin --profile web add .` from the repository root.\n\nTo try the plugin without installing it, run from the DSH checkout:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh --patch <path-to-this-repository>/cordis.source.patch.yml --no-open\n```\n\nFor a preview with deterministic test data:","source":"extracted","section":"Develop"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-8","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Develop：```sh\nnode scripts/build-preview.mjs\npython3 -m http.server 3468 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory dist/preview\n```","source":"extracted","section":"Develop"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-9","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Usage：- **Zoom**: drag across the overview to select a range; double-click to reset. The target icon on a turn focuses it.\n- **Live following**: running sessions open at the bottom. New rows stay in view while you remain there; scrolling up, searching, filtering errors, focusing a turn, or opening a summary pauses following. Scroll back to the bottom to resume. Historical sessions open at the top.\n- **Stable live axis**: the global view reserves space ahead of the latest call and expands in rounded blocks. Completed bars stay fixed between expansions; when the session ends, the axis fits the recorded end time. Manual zoom and turn focus keep their selected range.\n- **Search**: Ctrl/Cmd+F. Matches in names, arguments, prompts, and outputs are highlighted.\n- **Errors only**: lists failed operations with their parent context. A recovered failure adds an error badge to its turn instead of marking the whole turn red.\n- **Escape** closes the summary or details, or clears filters.","source":"extracted","section":"Usage"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-10","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · Notes：- Total tokens = uncached input + cache-read input + cache-write input + output, matching the DSH status bar. Cache hit rate is cache-read input divided by all input.\n- Idle gaps longer than 60 seconds are compressed; recorded durations are unchanged.\n- Independent child-agent sessions are not merged into the parent trace.\n- Cost is not shown, since recorded traces carry no authoritative pricing.\n- The plugin is presentation-only: it adds no tools, changes no agent behavior, and sends no telemetry.","source":"extracted","section":"Notes"}
{"unit_id":"omdsh-dev__dsh-trace-waterfall#readme-11","repo":"omdsh-dev/dsh-trace-waterfall","commit":"6c73e9a0a85d1ded06b088e0f1435d15dc278660","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-trace-waterfall README · License：The adapter modules derive from DSH's MIT-licensed trajectory implementation. See [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).","source":"extracted","section":"License"}
